.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt HANDLE_TRANSFER 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm handle_transfer
.Nd installs a handle in another process
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ft Handle
.Fn handle_transfer "Handle dest_proc" "Handle handle" "u32 rights_mask"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
installs an independent duplicate of
.Fa handle
in the handle table of the process named by
.Fa dest_proc .
The returned handle value is valid only in that destination table.
.Pp
.Fa dest_proc
must name a Process object and carry
.Dv WRITE .
.Fa handle
must carry
.Dv TRANSFER .
The new handle rights are the source rights intersected with the nonzero
.Fa rights_mask ;
rights never grow.
.Pp
Memory objects, SchemeFile objects, and SchemeServer objects are transferable.
Process, Namespace, and request handles are not transferable.
The source handle remains valid, and either process may close its own handle independently.
The kernel releases the source table lock before acquiring the destination table lock, including
when the destination is the caller.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
On success,
.Nm
returns the destination-table handle.
On failure it returns a negative error number.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADF
The source or destination handle is stale, or the source object kind is not transferable.
.It Bq Er EPERM
The destination Process lacks
.Dv WRITE
or the source handle lacks
.Dv TRANSFER .
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa rights_mask
is zero, or
.Fa dest_proc
does not name a Process object.
.It Bq Er EMFILE
The destination handle table is full.
.El
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
